-- title:
--   Lemma A.2: Pointed cone generated by a convex set avoiding zero
-- statement:
--   Let $C$ be a closed convex subset of a finite-dimensional real vector space $V$. If its translation recession cone $\operatorname{lim}(C)$ is pointed and $0\notin C$, then
--
--   $$\operatorname{cone}(C)\text{ is pointed}.$$
--
--   The generated cone is closed and contains zero; for nonempty convex $C$ it is $\overline{\mathbb R_{\ge0}C}$. For empty $C$ it is $\{0\}$, with no added nonemptiness hypothesis. This is the appendix cone-generation tool.
-- source:
--   Elements in pointed invariant cones in Lie algebras and corresponding affine pairs, arXiv:2110.07297v1, PDF p. 27, Lemma A.2: Pointed cone generated by a convex set avoiding zero

